WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.015
(light music)

00:00:01.015 --> 00:00:05.015
- [Narrator] This is
Kamaria, a milky eagle owl.

00:00:06.945 --> 00:00:08.568
The largest African owl,

00:00:08.568 --> 00:00:11.453
it is found throughout sub-Saharan Africa.

00:00:11.453 --> 00:00:14.596
The eagle in their name
refers to their large size.

00:00:14.596 --> 00:00:16.768
Females are much larger than males,

00:00:16.768 --> 00:00:19.268
sometimes over a third bigger.

00:00:20.364 --> 00:00:22.173
They feed on a large variety of animals

00:00:22.173 --> 00:00:27.049
everything from mammals, fish,
rodents and even large birds.

00:00:27.049 --> 00:00:29.647
They hunt from a perch
using their sharp vision

00:00:29.647 --> 00:00:31.690
to spot prey before flying in

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:35.093
and seizing them with
their powerful talons.

00:00:35.093 --> 00:00:36.446
While it is a dominant bird,

00:00:36.446 --> 00:00:38.969
its population has seen a decline

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:41.620
due to a combination of
loss of suitable habitat,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.501
hunting, disease and drought.

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:45.975
Their slow reproductive rate

00:00:45.975 --> 00:00:50.233
has made it difficult for the
population to recover quickly.

00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:52.566
This is the milky eagle owl.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.986
(light music)

